 "disclosures": [
  "Liftoff epoch equals the consumer's JD_LAUNCH literal (13:32:00.960 UTC) so the captured insertion and the re-fly share one epoch; the exact 13:32:00.000 build needs the insertion re-captured at that JD.",
  "Precession of date is evaluated exactly at every ephemeris call, as the re-homed consumer does since 2026-10-25 (its original memoised the matrix on 52.6-minute steps filled at the first query: Moon 0 to 9.6 m behind, 1.9 km at TEI ignition over the 55 h LOI-2 -> TEI coast); with the exact matrix the consumer reproduces this package's lunar coasts to 3.4 m.",
  "No midcourse corrections are modelled; MCC-2 (6.4 m/s as flown) and MCC-5 are the consumer's in-flight correctors.",
  "LM jettison and the CSM separation burn before TEI are not modelled; the TEI state is the post-LOI-2 CSM orbit propagated in the full model.",
  "The TLI is a free return (ballistic continuation enters at -6.49 deg on the 400 kft shell, return perigee 38 km) as Apollo 11 flew; the Site 2 plane is LOI-1's plane change (2.76 deg, as flown 4.1 deg), and the lunar parking orbit sits 2.19 deg from retrograde-equatorial (Apollo: 1.25 deg).",
  "The TLI arrival-phase pin (pericynthion longitude) is not solved (ill-posed with ignition angle and pitch both rotating the departure); the longitude is screened.",
  "The recovery zone is screened: the zone cross-track residual is ill-posed with perigee and time of flight pinned (zone near the Earth-Moon axis at entry). The TEI is solved in plane: the as-flown EI latitude is not reachable from the free-return capture orbit with the corridor FPA and the planned EI epoch (the hold bottoms out 0.4 deg / 2 min off against the no-entry edge with ~190 m/s out of plane vs the as-flown 81); EI latitude -9.64 deg (as flown -3.19) and zone crossrange +71 km are screened. GO_D_TARGET_KM is a placeholder.",
  "The free-return EI flight-path angle is solved on the return perigee radius of the osculating return conic (1 km of perigee ~ 0.04 deg); its corridor (-6.5 +/- 1 deg) is screened in free_return_screen.",
  "Descent, surface stay, ascent and rendezvous are the consumer's; the package gives the CSM orbit at the site-plane epoch and the slot's DOI GET.",
  "Entry (guidance to the zone) is the consumer's; the package gives the EI state and geometry."
 ],
